{"id":"u-bbba4c49-6026-4d19-88bf-8e152be35f06","src":"community","title":"Berry's Backsafe Bodybuilding","author":"Berry B.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/ZdZCTB-berrys-backsafe-bodybuilding","desc":"This program is designed for maximum muscle hypertrophy while remaining joint- and lower-back friendly, especially for lifters with a history of lower back issues.\n\nThe focus is on:\n- Mechanical tension as the primary driver of hypertrophy\n- Smart exercise selection (machines, chest-supported movements, controlled ROM)\n- Moderate to higher rep ranges to reduce axial loading and fatigue\n- RPE-based progression instead of mandatory training to failure\n\nThe program intentionally avoids excessive axial loading (e.g. heavy squats and deadlifts), while still training the entire posterior chain effectively through \nsafer alternatives. Your favorite core exercises can be added to e. g. day 4.\n\nStructure\n\n4 training days per week\n\nDay 1: Push\nDay 2: Lower (Back-Safe)\nDay 3: Pull\nDay 4: Posterior + Delts\n\n6-week training block\n\nWeeks 1–5: Progressive overload (double progression, typical target RPE 7–9)\n\nWeek 6: Deload (reduced volume and intensity)\nAuto-Regulation & Flexibility\n\nLifters may start lighter (e.g. RPE 6–7) if needed, especially during the first week or on low-energy days\nOn days with good recovery and joint comfort, sets may be pushed slightly harder (up to RPE 9), while maintaining proper technique.\n\nLoad and effort should always be adjusted based on day-to-day readiness.\n\nKey Principles\n- No mandatory training to failure\n- No maximal strength testing\n- Controlled range of motion where appropriate\n- Progress only if technique and joint comfort are maintained\n\nThis program is ideal for lifters who want to build muscle consistently, stay pain-free, and train in a sustainable, long-term manner.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Athletics"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":20,"rate":5,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-05-14T03:40:55.646Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push","Lower","Pull","Posterior + Delts"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Shoulder Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Leg Press (45 Degrees)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Squat (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single-Leg Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Calf Raise (Leg Press)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Neutral Grip)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single Arm Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":7.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"rpe":7.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"rpe":7.5,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Single-Leg Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pull Through (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"x":2}]},{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single Arm Rear Delt Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets"